The only person who has provided a patch where the skill for the offhand 
weapon plays any part in 2-weapon is me and I doubt that anybody else 
has ever tried it.

The only case where this would be a factor would be if you lost your 
primary weapon to a whip and in that case exchanging the offhand weapon 
in as your primary takes exactly as much time as choosing any other 
weapon to be your primary (modulo the Spork launcher autoready, which 
doesn't apply in this case).  In that case it is only the weight savings 
of having the off-hand weapon and emergency weapon as one item rather 
than two that applies.

Note that switching from 2-weapon to 1-weapon combat is always a zero 
time action and that switching the other way has only a 5% chance per DX 
under 20 of taking a move, which is gravy for a Rogue with DX 23 who 
just happens to have a primary weapon that inflicts scare.

Before I forget, there is one more "free" conversion from 2-weapon to 
1-weapon.  Throw the off hand weapon.  This doesn't help in Spork that 
much because the back toss has been nerfed away, but an emergency ranged 
weapon for d10+7 is always a nice trick to have in hand.  (Pun 
intended.)  And you can't do that with a saber against non-silver haters.

